{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cdlc35jb2hgicdvcxcc4sn2fsah4xavzwq27wv52agc5axvpkpfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What this project actually is\n\nThe task template assumed a multi-feature C *library*; the reality is much smaller, and that reshaped the work:\n\n- `c_src/src/main.c` is **5 non-comment lines** — `printf(\"Hello World!\\n\"); return 0;` — built by CMake as an **executable**, not a `.so`.\n- `Cargo.toml` had **no `[features]` table**, and CMakeLists has no `option()`/`#ifdef`, so the feature powerset is the **single empty set** (verified mechanically by `run_all_configs.sh`, not assumed). I ran it under both dev and release profiles instead, since `[profile.release]` sets `panic = \"abort\"`.\n\nTo satisfy the \"load both `.so`s via libloading\" requirement, `build.rs` compiles the *unmodified* C source a second way (`-shared -fPIC`) and builds a Rust `cdylib` from a new `src/lib.rs`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified.\n\n## The one real bug found\n\n**SIGPIPE handling** (`ERRORS.md` row E1). Rust's runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` before `main`, so with stdout on a pipe with no reader:\n\n| | C | Rust (before) | Rust (after) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| wait status | **141** (killed by signal 13) | 0 | **141** |\n\nFixed in `src/main.rs` by restoring `SIG_DFL` at process start. Crucially, that fix belongs to the *C runtime emulation*, **not** to the translated `main` body — the C library's `main` never touches signal dispositions, so the exported `.so` `main` in `src/lib.rs` deliberately leaves them alone. Row E2 pins that distinction down (host ignores SIGPIPE → discarded `EPIPE`, still returns 0). The logic lives in one shared `src/hello.rs` so the binary and the `.so` export cannot drift.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **SYMBOLS.md** — C `.so` exports exactly one symbol, `main`; Rust `.so` exports it too. Symbol diff **empty in both directions**, 0 unresolved non-libc symbols (`ldd -r` clean). No C source went untranslated.\n- [x] **CONFIGS.md** — 23 rows, all passing, with randomized inputs (fixed seed) for argv/env/file-prefix/stdin/call-count/interleave-order. Includes the low-level `.so` entry point, not just the executable: 100-call sequences, randomized C/Rust interleaving on one fd, real pty, `O_APPEND` over random prefixes, 32 concurrent processes, stdin-offset preservation.\n- [x] **ERRORS.md** — the C has **provably zero** explicit rejections (grep counts shown for 20 constructs, all 0). 8 implicit rows (E1–E8) + generic boundaries, each asserting the *same* signal/code/byte count, not merely \"both failed\". Out-of-range enums documented as genuinely N/A (no enum params) rather than silently skipped.\n- [x] **All under every feature combination** — 31 tests × dev/release, plus symbol parity per profile: `ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED`.\n\nTwo things worth flagging, since they'd otherwise look like passing-by-luck:\n\n1. **I validated the suite isn't vacuous** via mutation testing: removing the newline → 6 failures; removing the SIGPIPE fix → exactly `e1_sigpipe_killed`; making the export return 1 → 7 FFI failures.\n2. **One \"divergence\" was my own harness bug** — libtest's progress text leaked into a captured fd-1 buffer under parallel threads. I fixed the cause (`RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` in `.cargo/config.toml`) rather than filtering the captured bytes, which would have masked real output differences."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1095,"cache_read_input_tokens":138089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1095,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf729fa6-6a08-4dbd-999c-494779251cf1","uuid":"5c48d9b3-c515-4523-a0e0-7c88824df8a6","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:33:23.935Z"}
